{%- comment -%}
  BeFree design tokens — the single source for colour and type.

  Every BeFree section renders this snippet, so no component ever hard-codes a
  brand colour again. The greens all sit on hue 150.4 in OKLCH, which is the
  book cover's leather measured over 81% of its pixels; the golds sit on hue
  72.2, the dot in the logo. The package already moved to those hues, so the
  store matches the book, the two apps and the PDFs.

  Contrast, measured against --bf-cream:
    --bf-green-800 ink      11.00:1
    --bf-green-900 button   10.53:1   (--bf-cream-hi on it: 11.18:1)
    --bf-gold-ink            3.20:1   on cream, 3.29:1 on --bf-green-900
    --bf-gold                1.96:1   decorative only: rules, dots, never text

  Rendering it more than once per page is harmless — the declarations are
  identical and the browser keeps one copy of the stylesheet. At assembly the
  two <link> tags move to theme.liquid and this drops to the <style> alone.
{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,500;9..144,600&family=Poppins:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
<style>
  :root{
    --bf-cream:#F8F6EF;
    --bf-cream-hi:#FFFDF5;
    --bf-ring:#E8D1BA;
    --bf-green-900:#1F4127;
    --bf-green-800:#223D28;
    --bf-green-700:#1C4C2A;
    --bf-green-500:#447E52;
    --bf-gold:#EDA335;
    --bf-gold-ink:#BE7C00;
    --bf-display:Fraunces,Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif;
    --bf-sans:Poppins,system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",sans-serif;
    --bf-mono:"IBM Plex Mono",ui-monospace,monospace;
  }
</style>
